Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:57:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Use the browser already installed rather than downloading
 one

npx playwright install chromium fetches from cdn.playwright.dev, which the
university network blocks -- five attempts, each timing out after two minutes.
The download was never necessary. Edge and Chrome are the same engine as
Playwright's Chromium, and Playwright can drive either through a channel with
nothing downloaded at all. On Windows Edge is always present.

The script now tries Playwright's own Chromium first, then chrome, then
msedge, and reports which it used. --browser forces one. When none can be
launched the error names each candidate and what went wrong with it, rather
than failing with a stack trace about a zip file.

Which browser took the figures is written into FIGURES.md alongside the
viewport and device scale, because the figures are meant to be reproducible
and "a Chromium browser" is not a reproducible statement.

Checked: the fallback launches the bundled Chromium where one exists, and a
forced-but-absent channel produces the intended message naming the channel.

